{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858291-sleeping-and-reverting-to-one-s-breed-form","id":858291,"title":"Sleeping and reverting to one's breed form","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-03T05:36:11-07:00","id":858291,"title":"Sleeping and reverting to one's breed form","content":"When Garou fall asleep in another form do they shift back to their breed form? I used to run it that characters could spend willpower to stay in another form while asleep but I'd like to know if there is a cannon answer. Thanks for you help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T07:14:35-07:00","id":858327,"title":"","content":"Id also like an answer to this... if they auto transform back when asleep, its ... Difficult to say the least, for a lupus to &quot;Experiment with living in human society.&quot; <br /> <br /> And makes the specialized Rite to change ones effective breed form, NOT AT ALL optional for Rokea betweeners.<br /> <br /> I usualy let them stay transformed as incapacitated is a bit more unconcious then asleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T11:06:10-07:00","id":858407,"title":"","content":"I've seen it houseruled like that. But as far as I know, if you can sleep in non-breedform just fine. After all, falling asleep is a process, not a quick thing like being knocked out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:25:27-07:00","id":858443,"title":"","content":"They do take their breed form when they sleep. The Rokea have a rite to stop this from happening because this happening to them can be fatal. It worth noting that when Rokea use this rite without a good reason they lose renown for it. Garou who act outside there Auspice/Breed are often punished much the same way, so if a lupus was to learn some way to exist outside of breed form, they should also receive a similar punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:31:45-07:00","id":858448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858291-sleeping-and-reverting-to-one-s-breed-form?p=858443#post858443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do take their breed form when they sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this in the rules? I don't remember anything like this. I know you mentioned a rite of the Rokea so I assume it's mentioned in reference to them. But what about in the core rules for Garou, not the other changing breeds?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:54:06-07:00","id":858463,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I swear it used to say that if a Garou goes unconscious they revert to breed form. After reading page 255 of the W20 I don't think that is the case. It states that a Garou knocked out by bashing damage remains in the form she was in prior to being knocked out, only being knocked out with lethal damage reverts her to breed form. Based I that I would have to say that they can sleep in which ever form they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T13:08:15-07:00","id":858471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858291-sleeping-and-reverting-to-one-s-breed-form?p=858463#post858463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I swear it used to say that if a Garou goes unconscious they revert to breed form. After reading page 255 of the W20 I don't think that is the case. It states that a Garou knocked out by bashing damage remains in the form she was in prior to being knocked out, only being knocked out with lethal damage reverts her to breed form. Based I that I would have to say that they can sleep in which ever form they want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With this in W20 I'd say sleeping in your breed form would also be allowed. Maybe the rite for the Rokea exists because they have so little human blood in their spiritual lineage so the homid form is just that much harder for them to maintain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T13:42:13-07:00","id":858501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858291-sleeping-and-reverting-to-one-s-breed-form?p=858443#post858443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so if a lupus was to learn some way to exist outside of breed form, they should also receive a similar punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does limit what a lupus can do a lot, not to mention a metis. They do have to blend into the human society sometimes, even if because pack is on a mission in the city.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T13:50:43-07:00","id":858503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858291-sleeping-and-reverting-to-one-s-breed-form?p=858471#post858471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With this in W20 I'd say sleeping in your breed form would also be allowed. Maybe the rite for the Rokea exists because they have so little human blood in their spiritual lineage so the homid form is just that much harder for them to maintain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how high level a rite it is, it's one damned huge Air-Breathing Mermaid hurdle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T14:01:46-07:00","id":858509,"title":"","content":"The Rite exists and is necessary for the for the Rokea because it effectively changes their breed form in all cases not just sleeping. So, if they lose the shark or are knocked unconscious with lethal damage they revert to the form they have chosen, not squamus. A lupus beaten unconscious would still revert to lupus and have some explaining to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T14:25:45-07:00","id":858529,"title":"","content":"I would rule from my experience that sleeping or being knocked unconscious would render a Garou back to their breed form, only death can do that. However I would argue from a roleplay perspective that a Garou couldnt sleep in Chrinos with the exception of Metis. The Rage that resides in the War Form would be too great, kind of how it hard to sleep when your mind is racing. Metis can do this from years of practice. My little boy is 20 months old and it takes him forever to sleep at bedtime, somethings rolling around his cot for hours. Imagine that for a baby Metis would could stay away for days before exhaustion took them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T16:24:31-07:00","id":858591,"title":"","content":"...granted the CoG revised book does have that lupus with the boyfriend and has him wake up in lupus form after a night of &quot;fun&quot;...(don't kill me for citing it! I just couldn't resist!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T19:55:35-07:00","id":858692,"title":"","content":"In earlier editions, being knocked unconscious would revert you to breed form. It never mentioned falling asleep.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven that rule was relaxed for 3rd ed, and IIRC, keeping form was a WP roll.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T22:48:59-07:00","id":858785,"title":"","content":"Hello All,<br /> <br /> I must state, based on my education / experience, that who sleeps doesn't become unconscious, (But alcohol poisoning could be, so avoid russian vodka!)<br /> <br /> I hope this solves the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T04:02:29-07:00","id":858872,"title":"","content":"There are two distinct mentions, that one does not revert back to breed form.<br /> Wendigo 1st Edition book states that there is rite that needs to be in lupus form to survive harsh conditions for several days. Ergo, one can sleep in the form one falls asleep in.<br /> <br /> More prominent is the rule, that one may not shapeshift if pregnant in the third trimester. Since revised the child is of the mothers breed, which is the form one has to be in, so no biggie, unless one is pregnant with a metis. A mother in this case has to be in crinos form for months, even while asleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T05:59:24-07:00","id":858930,"title":"","content":"Hey Heinrich,<br /> <br /> I always envy your logical reasoning based on in game materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T18:52:02-07:00","id":859380,"title":"","content":"You would absolutely not revert to breed form just for going to sleep. <br /> <br /> World of darkness is built around the idea that the veil/masquerade/shroud/purple curtain of goo should not be broken and all reality deviants are naturally inclined to maintain these rules. It'd be such a canonical mess if just regular sleep caused shift changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T20:07:36-07:00","id":859414,"title":"","content":"Another point that says you can sleep in other forms is is the mokole breed book. They have archid traits like storing fat in your tail or storing food in the crop. It feels like these wouldn't be worth much (especially the tail) unless you could sleep in that form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T21:04:07-07:00","id":859445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858291-sleeping-and-reverting-to-one-s-breed-form?p=859414#post859414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another point that says you can sleep in other forms is is the mokole breed book. They have archid traits like storing fat in your tail or storing food in the crop. It feels like these wouldn't be worth much (especially the tail) unless you could sleep in that form.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then again, if a Mokole is going to be sleeping for a long time, they're probably going to use the Gift or rite that allows them to sleep in suspended animation with no need for food, and which I think has a specific clause for allowing you to sleep in Archid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T22:14:42-07:00","id":875290,"title":"","content":"I've always ran it most fera can sleep in what ever form they are in.. Only rokea and Corax have to shift to breed form before hand...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T23:58:37-07:00","id":875378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858291-sleeping-and-reverting-to-one-s-breed-form?p=875290#post875290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always ran it most fera can sleep in what ever form they are in.. Only rokea and Corax have to shift to breed form before hand...</div> </div> </div> </div>Rokea in shark form can't properly be said to sleep like a human, though. It's a progressive &quot;power down&quot; across different portions of the brain that still leaves enough activity to swim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T00:53:56-07:00","id":875409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858291-sleeping-and-reverting-to-one-s-breed-form?p=875378#post875378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rokea in shark form can't properly be said to sleep like a human, though. It's a progressive &quot;power down&quot; across different portions of the brain that still leaves enough activity to swim.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is a sufficient substitute, for ingame purposes. They normally can't sleep in homid-form, as they need to constantly be in motion (and sleeping on a train doesn't count). So, they go into the water and power down parts of their brains instead.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}